WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.712
Reshaping changes the dimensions of an array while keeping the same underlying values.

00:00:05.712 --> 00:00:12.852
For example, six values in a one-dimensional array can be reshaped into two rows and three columns,

00:00:12.852 --> 00:00:16.054
as long as the total number of elements stays the same.

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:21.630
Transposing swaps rows and columns in a two-dimensional array.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:29.010
If we start with three rows and two columns, the transpose will have two rows and three columns.

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:36.630
These operations are useful when a model, algorithm, or calculation expects data in a particular shape.

00:00:36.630 --> 00:00:43.185
Before reshaping, check the current size and think about what the new rows and columns will represent.
